Original commit body from c8691b5f4c34360c80b5d7ebb52660d29e18f609:

Ruby resolves a relative constant through Module.nesting before the top
level, so Orchestrator inside module TestData is TestData::Orchestrator.
_try_receiver_call tried only the name as written, and a class declared
compactly (class TestData::Orchestrator) is registered only under its
full name, so the in-repo call fell to constant_external (chatwoot
lib/test_data.rb).

_lexical_nesting reads the call site's enclosing module / class nodes
(positional, innermost first; a compact class A::C is one level, as in
Ruby), and _nested_candidates puts each nesting-qualified name ahead of
the written one, in the method lookup and in the .new -> #initialize
path. Only exact registered keys match; an absolute ::X gets none.

